# @name: aws | Add Inbound Rule to Security Group
# @description: Adds an inbound rule to a security group Group: AWS EC2 Commands. Template: replace placeholders before running. {group_id} = The ID of the security group | {protocol} = The protocol (e.g., tcp, udp, icmp) [default "tcp"] | {port} = The port number or range (e.g., 22, 80, 443) | {cidr_ip} = The CIDR IP range (e.g., 0.0.0.0/0) [default "0.0.0.0/0"]
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress --group-id {group_id} --protocol {protocol} --port {port} --cidr {cidr_ip}